# Pending human-applied patch — issue #731 (PM gate② finding + independent-reviewer gate② P1
# (sol), PR #818)
#
# WHAT: extends guard.ts's Bash-argument accident fence to recognize the three stop-control
#       CLI verbs #731 shipped — `sapwood pause`, `sapwood stop`, `sapwood estop` (activate AND
#       `clear` forms) — as human-merge-only, the SAME boundary CONTROL_SENTINEL_RE already
#       enforces for the raw files (data/PAUSE, data/KILL_SWITCH, data/EMERGENCY_STOP). Adds one
#       new function pair (isSapwoodCliEntrypoint / checkStopControlVerb) wired into
#       judgeFragment, plus a BLOCK/ALLOW test matrix in guard.test.ts. Scope is deliberately
#       minimal (大道至简): ONLY the three stop-control verbs, activate and clear forms — `park`/
#       `run`/`status`/`events` are explicitly OUT of scope (a worker has ordinary legitimate
#       reason to invoke those; widening this rule to every subcommand is a non-goal, not an
#       oversight — the ALLOW matrix below proves it). Recognizes the DISCOVERABLE entrypoint
#       forms only: the bare `sapwood` binary, `node .../cli.js`/`cli.ts` (path-prefixed or
#       direct-executed), and `npx sapwood[@version]` (npm's own documented "run a specific/
#       latest version" syntax). Deliberately does NOT chase adversarial forms that hide the
#       command word behind an arbitrary package spec (`npx --offline file:<path>/engine`, a
#       scoped `@scope/pkg`, an aliased binary) — an accepted, documented residual, same class as
#       checkControlSentinelArg's own "hardcoded path inside a script" residual. Full design
#       rationale (why each bypass class was/wasn't closed) lives in docs/security.md's
#       "Sentinel isolation boundary" section — not duplicated here.
#
# WHY IT IS A PATCH AND NOT A COMMIT: engine/src/guard/** is human-merge-only (CLAUDE.md
#       "Non-negotiables"; canonical list docs/security.md "Human-merge-only paths"). An
#       autonomous worker's write to guard.ts/guard.test.ts is denied at the tool level:
#         BLOCK [write-path] guard/reviewer/merge-driver source is human-merge-only
#       The guard constrains Claude tool calls, never a human's editor.
#
# APPLY (from the repo root), then delete this file AND its apply-check test:
#       git apply docs/patches/731-guard-stop-control-verbs.patch
#       git rm docs/patches/731-guard-stop-control-verbs.patch
#       git rm engine/src/guard/patch-731-apply-check.test.ts
#       # ^ that test's whole job is proving THIS patch applies cleanly pre-apply; once applied,
#       #   the patch file it asserts existsSync() on is gone (by the git rm two lines up), so the
#       #   test would fail on every future CI run if left behind — remove it, don't make it
#       #   skip-when-absent (a passing-by-vacuity test is worse than no test).
#       npm --workspace engine test    # exercises the new BLOCK/ALLOW rows this patch adds
#
# NOTE: this patch's guard.ts hunk is positioned away from #679's own guard.ts hunk (docs/patches/
#       679-guard-default-branch-push.patch, if applying both) — both apply cleanly in either
#       order; see this PR's body for the both-orders `git apply --check` proof.
